\v 27 This is¦4646 the¦4646 record of¦4646 Terah's¦4647 descendants: Terah's¦4648 sons were¦4646 Abram¦4652, Nahor¦4655, and¦4656 Haran¦4658 and¦4659 Haran¦4659 had \add a son named\add* Lot¦4663.
\v 28 While¦4670 his¦4671 father¦4671 was still alive, Haran¦4666 died¦4665 in the land¦4672 where he¦4665 was born, in \add the city of\add* Ur¦4674 where the¦4675 Chaldeans¦4675 lived.
\v 29 Meanwhile Abram¦4678 married Sarai¦4686 and Nahor¦4679 married Milcah. (Milcah and \add her sister\add* Iscah¦4699 were the¦4682 daughters¦4692 of¦4682 \add Nahor's brother\add* Haran¦4694.)
\v 30 However, Sarai¦4702 wasn't able to¦4705 get pregnant \add so they\add* didn't¦4704 have any children¦4706.
\p
\v 31 Then¦4708 one day, Terah¦4709 gathered his son Abram¦4727 and his grandson Lot¦4716 (who was Haran's¦4719 son), and¦4723 his¦4725 daughter-in-law¦4725 Sarai¦4724 (who was Abram's¦4712 wife¦4726), and¦4729 they¦4729 \add all\add* left¦4729 from¦4731 \add the city of\add* Ur¦4731 (where the¦4732 Chaldeans¦4732 lived¦4740), to travel¦4733 to the region¦4734 of¦4735 Canaan¦4735, \add but\add* when they¦4736 arrived¦4736 at \add the city of\add* Haran¦4739, they¦4740 \add decided to\add* live¦4740 there¦4741.
\v 32 Then¦4743 when Terah¦4746 was¦4743 205 years¦4748 old, he¦4751 \add died\add* there in¦4753 Haran¦4753.
\c 12
