\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦4757 said¦4756 to¦4758 Abram¦4760, “You must¦4767 leave¦4761 your land¦4764 and¦4765 your relatives and¦4766 your¦4767 father's¦4767 house¦4766 and go¦4761 to the¦4770 land¦4770 that¦4771 I'll¦4767 show¦4772 you.\x + \xo 12:1: \xt Acts 7:2-3; Heb 11:8.\x*
\v 2 I'll bless¦4777 you and make you into a great¦4776 nation¦4775. I'll make¦4778 you famous and¦4780 you'll be¦4780 a blessing¦4781 \add to others\add*.
\v 3 I'll bless¦4783 everyone¦4789 who blesses¦4783 you, but¦4783 I'll curse¦4786 anyone who curses¦4786 you. All¦4789 the¦4790 families¦4790 on the earth will¦4783 be¦4787 blessed¦4787 because of¦4789 you.\x + \xo 12:3: \xt Gal 3:8.\x*
\p
\v 4 So¦4793 Abram left \add there\add* just¦4795 as¦4795 Yahweh¦4798 had¦4796 told¦4796 him, and¦4793 Lot¦4801 \add also\add* went¦4799 with¦4800 him¦4800. Abram was¦4803 seventy-five¦4807 years¦4806 old when he¦4796 left \add the city of\add* Haran¦4810.
\v 5 He¦4812 took¦4812 his¦4817 wife¦4817 Sarai¦4816 and¦4818 his nephew Lot¦4820 and¦4824 all¦4826 their¦4828 possessions¦4828 that¦4829 they had¦4830 accumulated¦4830 and¦4831 the people¦4833 who¦4834 they¦4836 had¦4836 acquired¦4836 in¦4837 Haran¦4837, and¦4838 they¦4838 set out¦4838 to¦4839 go¦4839 to the land¦4840 of¦4841 Canaan¦4841.
\p When¦4812 they¦4830 arrived¦4842 in the¦4833 Canaan region¦4840,
\v 6 they continued travelling¦4846 as far as the¦4848 city of¦4850 Shekem¦4851, to¦4852 Moreh's¦4854 oak tree¦4853. (The¦4850 Canaanites were still living in that region at that time.)
\v 7 Then¦4859 Yahweh came to¦4861 Abram and¦4864 told¦4864 him, “I'll¦4866 give¦4866 this¦4870 land¦4869 to your¦4865 descendants¦4865.” So¦4859 Abram built¦4871 an¦4873 altar¦4873 there¦4872 \add and made a burnt offering\add* to¦4874 Yahweh, who¦4875 had¦4875 appeared¦4875 to¦4876 him¦4876.\x + \xo 12:7: \xt Acts 7:5; Gal 3:16.\x*
\v 8 Then¦4878 from¦4879 there he¦4878 went¦4878 on¦4878 to¦4880 the hills¦4880 to the east¦4881 of¦4882 Beyt-El (Beyt-El¦4882) and¦4885 pitched¦4885 his¦4886 tents¦4886, with Beyt¦4888-El¦4890 on the¦4891 west¦4891 and¦4892 Ai¦4892 on the¦4892 east¦4893. He¦4894 built¦4894 an¦4897 altar¦4897 to¦4898 Yahweh there, and¦4899 \add sacrificed and\add* prayed to Yahweh
\v 9 before continuing¦4906 \add south down\add* toward¦4907 the¦4907 Negev¦4904 \add desert\add*.
\s1 Abram goes to Egypt
