\p
\v 10 \add One time when\add* there was¦4910 \add a drought causing\add* a severe food shortage, Abram¦4914 \add and his household\add* travelled \add west\add* across to¦4915 Egypt¦4915 \add !(Mitsrayim¦4915)\add* to¦4916 stay¦4916 there¦4917.
\v 11 Just¦4925 before they arrived in Mitsrayim¦4928, \add Abram\add* said¦4929 to¦4927 his¦4933 wife¦4933 Sarai¦4932, “Listen, you're a¦4939 very beautiful¦4940 woman¦4939,
\v 12 so when the¦4950 Egyptians¦4950 see¦4948 you¦4949 they'll say¦4951, ‘This¦4953 is¦4945 his¦4952 wife¦4952,’ and¦4945 they'll kill¦4954 me¦4955 but¦4945 let¦4957 you live¦4957.
\v 13 \add Please\add* tell them that¦4964 you're my¦4962 sister¦4962 so¦4964 they'll treat me well¦4965 because¦4968 of¦4968 you¦4968 and¦4969 let me live¦4969.”\x + \xo 12:13: \xt Gen 20:2; 26:7.\x*
\v 14 So¦4973 that's¦4982 what happened when they¦4977 entered¦4974 Mitsrayim¦4976—the Egyptians \add indeed\add* noticed¦4977 that Sarai was¦4984 very¦4986 beautiful¦4984,
\v 15 and¦4988 \add when\add* Far'oh's \add !(Pharaoh's¦4991)\add* officials¦4990 saw¦4988 her, so they¦4988 told him \add about her beauty\add*, and she¦4997 was¦4997 taken¦4997 into Far'oh's \add palace\add*.
\v 16 He¦5003 treated Abram¦5002 well \add (thinking he was the brother)\add*, so he¦5005 \add was given\add* flocks¦5008 and¦5010 herds¦5010, male and female donkeys¦5011, male¦5012 and female slaves, and camels¦5015.
\p
\v 17 \add But\add* Yahweh¦5018 directed terrible \add ≈deadly¦5023 diseases¦5023\add* onto Far'oh¦5022 and¦5025 his household¦5027 \add because of his taking\add* Abram's¦5033 wife¦5032 Sarai¦5031.
\v 18 So¦5035 Far'oh¦5036 called¦5035 for¦5043 Abram¦5037 and¦5035 said¦5038, “What's¦5039 this¦5041 you've done¦5042 to¦5043 me¦5043? Why didn't¦5045 you¦5047 tell¦5047 me that¦5041 she's¦5051 your¦5050 wife¦5050?
\v 19 Why¦5062 did¦5054 you¦5054 say¦5054, ‘She's¦5056 my¦5055 sister¦5055,’ so that I¦5057 took¦5057 her¦5058 in as a¦5060 wife? Now¦5061 then, here's¦5062 your¦5063 wife. Take¦5064 her and¦5061 get¦5064 out of¦5055 here.”
\v 20 Then¦5067 Far'oh¦5069 commanded¦5067 his \add officers\add*, and¦5071 they¦5071 sent¦5071 Abram and¦5073 his¦5075 wife¦5075 away¦5071 and¦5076 everything that¦5080 belonged to¦5082 him¦5082.
\c 13
