\p
\v 1 Then¦5084 Abram¦5085 left Egypt¦5086 with¦5095 his¦5088 wife¦5088 and¦5089 everything that¦5091 belonged to¦5093 him¦5093, and¦5094 \add their nephew\add* Lot¦5094. \add They returned\add* to the¦5096 Negev
\v 2 and¦5098 \add now\add* Abram had become very¦5100 wealthy¦5099, with¦5101 \add both\add* livestock¦5101, and silver¦5102 and¦5103 gold¦5103.
\v 3 Then¦5105 they continued \add north\add* through the¦5107 Negev¦5107 as far as Beyt¦5110-El¦5112, to¦5113 the¦5115 place¦5115 where¦5116 his¦5120 tents¦5120 had¦5118 been¦5118 at¦5122 the beginning¦5122—between Beyt-El and¦5105 Ai¦5128—
\v 4 to¦5130 the¦5132 place¦5132 where he'd previously built¦5136 an altar¦5133,\x + \xo 13:4: \xt Gen 12:8.\x* and¦5139 Abram¦5141 \add sacrificed and\add* prayed to Yahweh¦5143 there¦5140.
\p
\v 5 Now Lot¦5147, who¦5148 was¦5148 travelling¦5148 with¦5149 Abram¦5151, also¦5145 had flocks¦5153 and¦5155 herds¦5155 and¦5156 tents¦5156,
\v 6 but¦5158 the¦5162 land¦5162 couldn't support¦5160 them¦5161 \add all\add* while they stayed¦5163 together¦5173. Because¦5161 \add the needs of\add* their¦5168 combined assets were¦5171 so \add demanding\add*, they couldn't all \add thrive\add* in one place
\v 7 and¦5175 that led to strife between¦5178 Abram's¦5182 and¦5183 Lot's¦5187 herdsmen¦5184. Also¦5175, the Canaanites¦5188 and¦5189 the¦5189 Perizzites¦5189 were¦5191 living¦5191 in the¦5192 land¦5192 at that time.
\p
\v 8 So¦5194 Abram¦5195 said¦5194 to¦5196 Lot¦5198, “Let's¦5202 not¦5199 have quarrelling between you¦5205 and¦5206 I, or between¦5206 yours herdsmen¦5207 and¦5208 mine, because¦5210 we're \add relatives\add*.
\v 9 Isn't the whole¦5217 land¦5219 available to¦5220 you? So let's separate¦5221. If¦5224 you go to the left then I'll go right¦5227, or if¦5228 you go to the right then I'll go left¦5231.”
\v 10 Lot¦5235 looked¦5239 \add all around\add* and saw¦5239 that¦5246 all the plain¦5244 of¦5244 the¦5245 Yordan¦5245 \add river valley\add* was¦5248 well-watered¦5248 through towards Tso'ar, \add just\add* like Yahweh's¦5252 garden¦5259 \add had been\add* before¦5249 he¦5233 destroyed¦5251 Sodom¦5255 and¦5256 Amorah¦5258 \add !(Gomorrah¦5258)\add*, and like the land¦5262 of¦5262 Egypt¦5263.\x + \xo 13:10: \xt Gen 2:10.\x*
\v 11 Lot¦5270 chose¦5267 all¦5272 of¦5272 the Yordan¦5275 plain¦5274 for himself, and¦5276 so he¦5276 travelled to¦5269 the east¦5278 and¦5279 they¦5279 separated¦5279 from¦5281 each¦5272 other.
\v 12 \add So\add* Abram¦5284 settled in¦5286 the land¦5286 of¦5286 Canaan¦5288, and¦5289 Lot¦5289 settled in¦5291 the¦5291 cities¦5291 of¦5291 the¦5292 plain¦5292 and¦5293 moved¦5293 his tents¦5293 as far as Sodom¦5296.
\v 13 \add However,\add* the¦5298 people¦5298 of¦5298 Sodom¦5299 were¦5300 extremely wicked¦5300, \add constantly\add* disobeying Yahweh¦5302.
\s1 God promises Abram the land
