\p
\v 5 Then¦5462 in¦5462 the fourteenth year¦5464, Kedorlaomer¦5466 and¦5467 the¦5467 kings¦5467 who¦5468 were with¦5462 him¦5469 went¦5465 and¦5470 attacked¦5470 the¦5473 Refaim¦5473 in¦5474 Ashteroth¦5474-Karnaim¦5475, and¦5476 the¦5478 Zuzim¦5478 in¦5479 Ham¦5479, and¦5480 the¦5481 Emim¦5481 in¦5482 Shaveh¦5482-Kiriathaim¦5483,
\v 6 and¦5485 the¦5487 Horites¦5487 in¦5488 the hill¦5488 country¦5488 of¦5488 Se'ir¦5489 as far as El¦5491 Paran¦5492, which¦5493 is¦5494 near the¦5496 wilderness¦5496.
\v 7 Then¦5498 \add those four kings\add* turned¦5498 back¦5498 and¦5499 went¦5499 to¦5500 En¦5502 Mishpat¦5503 (also called Kadesh¦5505) and they¦5499 attacked¦5506 the entire¦5509 territories¦5511 of¦5511 the¦5512 Amalekites¦5512 and¦5513 also¦5513 the¦5516 Amorites¦5516, who¦5517 were¦5517 living¦5517 in¦5518 Hazezon¦5518 Tamar¦5519.
\p
\v 8 Then¦5521 the¦5522 king¦5522 of Sodom¦5524, the¦5525 king¦5525 of¦5525 Amorah¦5526 \add !(Gomorrah¦5526)\add*, the¦5527 king¦5527 of¦5527 Admah¦5528, the¦5529 king¦5529 of¦5529 Tsevoim¦5530, and¦5532 the¦5532 king¦5532 of¦5532 Bela¦5533 (also¦5525 called Zoar¦5536) went¦5521 out¦5521 into¦5540 the Siddim¦5541 Valley¦5540 and arranged \add their troops\add* for battle¦5539
\v 9 against Kedorlaomer¦5544 king¦5545 of¦5545 Elam¦5546, Tidal¦5547 king¦5548 of¦5548 Goiim¦5549, Amrafel¦5550 king¦5551 of¦5551 Shinar¦5552, Arioch¦5553 king¦5554 of¦5554 Ellasar¦5555—five¦5560 kings¦5557 \add defending themselves\add* against the¦5560 four¦5556.
\v 10 Now the Siddim¦5563 Valley¦5562 had many tar pits, and¦5568 when the¦5569 kings¦5569 of¦5569 Sodom¦5571 and¦5572 Amorah¦5572 \add !(Gomorrah¦5572)\add* fled, they¦5578 fell¦5573 into¦5575 the pits, \add but\add* the rest fled up into¦5575 the¦5577 hills¦5577.
