\v 12 Abram's¦5605 nephew Lot¦5598 and¦5595 all his¦5601 possessions¦5601 also¦5599 got¦5595 taken¦5595 because he¦5607 was¦5608 living¦5608 in¦5609 \add the city of\add* Sodom¦5609,
\v 13 \add but\add* someone who escaped¦5612 came¦5611 and¦5613 reported¦5613 \add this news\add* to¦5614 Abram the¦5615 Hebrew¦5615. \add At that time,\add* Abram was¦5617 \add still\add* living¦5617 by the¦5618 terebinth trees¦5618 of¦5618 Mamre¦5619 the¦5620 Amorite¦5620, the¦5621 brother¦5621 of¦5621 Eshcol¦5622 and¦5623 the¦5623 brother¦5623 of¦5623 Aner¦5624, and¦5625 the three of them had formed an alliance \add together\add*.
\v 14 When¦5637 Abram¦5632 heard¦5631 that¦5633 his¦5635 nephew had¦5634 been¦5634 taken¦5634 captive¦5634, he led¦5634 out¦5636 his¦5639 318 trained¦5639 men¦5639 who'd \add all\add* been born¦5640 in his¦5641 house¦5641, and¦5631 he pursued¦5646 his enemies as far as \add the town of\add* Dan¦5649.
\v 15 During the night¦5654, Abram split¦5651 in his¦5656 slaves into groups and¦5657 they attacked¦5657 \add the four kings and their soldiers\add* and¦5658 pursued¦5658 them¦5658 to¦5659 Hobah¦5661 (north¦5663 of¦5664 Damascus¦5664).
\v 16 They were able to bring¦5666 back¦5666 all¦5668 the¦5670 possessions¦5670, as well as his nephew Lot¦5674 and¦5676 his¦5676 possessions, and¦5678 also¦5678 the¦5681 women¦5681 and¦5682 the¦5684 \add other\add* people¦5684 \add who'd been captured\add*.
