\v 2 “My¦5856 master¦5849 Yahweh¦5850,” replied¦5847 Abram¦5848, “what¦5851 will¦5853 you¦5853 give¦5853 me¦5855, since we have no children¦5858 and¦5847 it's¦5847 Eliezer¦5865 (\add my chief slave\add* from Damascus¦5864) who'll inherit all my possessions¦5861?”
\v 3 Then¦5867 he¦5867 continued¦5867, “\add Yes,\add* you¦5872 haven't given¦5872 me¦5870 a child¦5873 so wow, my¦5877 heir is¦5878 a slave from my household¦5877!”
\p
\v 4 Then¦5881 listen, Yahweh's¦5884 word¦5882 came¦5894 to¦5885 \add Abram\add* saying¦5886, “That¦5893 man won't¦5887 be your heir, but¦5881 on the¦5882 contrary, it'll be your biological son.”
\v 5 Then \add Yahweh\add* took¦5899 \add Abram\add* outside¦5901 and¦5902 said¦5902, “Look¦5903 up at the¦5906 sky¦5906 and see¦5903 if¦5909 you¦5911 can count¦5912 the stars¦5908.” Then he¦5914 said¦5914 to¦5915 him¦5915, “Your¦5918 descendants¦5918 will¦5917 be¦5917 like that.”\x + \xo 15:5: \xt Rom 4:18; Heb 11:12.\x*
\p
\v 6 \add Abram\add* believed¦5920 in¦5921 Yahweh¦5921, and¦5922 \add Yahweh considered that faith of Abram's as an act of obedience\add*.\x + \xo 15:6: \xt Rom 4:3; Gal 3:6; Jam 2:23.\x*
\p
\v 7 Then¦5926 Yahweh told¦5926 \add Abram\add*, “I'm¦5928 Yahweh who¦5930 brought¦5931 you¦5931 out¦5931 of¦5933 Ur¦5932 (where the¦5933 Chaldeans¦5933 lived) so I¦5931 could give¦5934 you this¦5939 land¦5938 to¦5940 possess¦5940 it¦5940.”
