\v 8 “My¦5943 master¦5943 Yahweh¦5944,” Abram asked¦5942, “how¦5945 will¦5946 I know¦5946 that¦5947 I will¦5948 possess¦5948 it¦5948?”
\p
\v 9 “Bring¦5952 me¦5953 a three-year-old heifer¦5954,” Yahweh replied¦5950, “and¦5956 a three-year-old¦5957 she-goat and¦5958 a three-year-old ram¦5958 and¦5960 a turtledove¦5960 and¦5961 a young¦5961 pigeon¦5961.”
\v 10 So¦5963 \add Abram\add* brought¦5963 all¦5968 those¦5970 to \add Yahweh\add*, and then¦5963 he¦5985 cut¦5971 the animals (but¦5963 not¦5984 the birds¦5982) in¦5973 half down the middle¦5973 and¦5974 laid the halves opposite¦5978 to each¦5968 other.
\v 11 Then¦5993 \add some\add* birds¦5988 of prey¦5988 flew down to the¦5988 carcasses¦5991, \add but\add* Abram¦5994 shooed them¦5993 away¦5992.
\p
