\v 39 \add Thus\add* the¦14279 flocks¦14279 would mate by the¦14282 \add striped\add* branches¦14282, and¦14283 \add they\add* would bear¦14283 young who were¦14278 streaked¦14285, speckled¦14286, and¦14287 spotted¦14287.
\p
\v 40 Then¦14289 Yacob¦14291 \add separated out those young animals into a separate flock\add*, and¦14292 he¦14292 made¦14303 the \add older\add* flocks look at¦14301 the streaked¦14297 and¦14298 all¦14298 the¦14301 dark-coloured animals in¦14301 Lavan's flocks¦14301. \add So\add* he¦14303 kept his own flocks by themselves and¦14308 didn't¦14308 \add mix\add* them¦14309 with¦14301 Lavan's flocks.
