\v 41 So¦14315 whenever the strong¦14320 animals were \add ready to mate\add*, then¦14315 Yacob¦14322 put¦14321 the¦14325 branches¦14325 in the troughs¦14328 \add in front\add* of¦14319 the flocks so that they would mate by the branches¦14330,
\v 42 \add but\add* when¦14332 the¦14333 animals were weak, he¦14335 didn't¦14334 put¦14335 them¦14335 in¦14332. So¦14332 the¦14337 weak animals went to¦14338 Lavan¦14338 and¦14332 the¦14339 strong¦14339 ones¦14337 to¦14340 Yacob¦14340
\v 43 so he¦14342 \add became very wealthy\add*, and¦14346 he¦14346 owned large flocks¦14349 \add as well as\add* male¦14352 and female¦14351 slaves, and camels¦14353 and¦14354 donkeys¦14354.
\c 31
