\p
\v 1 \add One day, Yacob\add* overheard the¦14359 words¦14359 of¦14360 Lavan's¦14362 sons¦14360 who were saying¦14363, “Yacob¦14365 has taken¦14364 everything that¦14371 belonged to our father, and¦14356 from¦14371 what \add originally\add* belonged¦14372 to¦14372 our father he¦14373 has¦14373 gained all¦14375 this¦14378 wealth¦14377.”
\v 2 Then¦14380 Yacob¦14381 \add also noticed\add* that Lavan's¦14385 \add attitude towards him had changed\add*, and¦14386 he¦14387 wasn't \add in favour of him like he'd been in the past\add*.
\v 3 Then¦14392 Yahweh¦14393 \add ≈told¦14392\add* Yacob¦14396, “Go back to¦14398 the¦14400 land¦14400 of¦14400 your ancestors¦14401 and¦14402 to¦14402 your relatives¦14402, and¦14403 I'll¦14403 be¦14403 with¦14404 you¦14404.”
\p
\v 4 \add So\add* Yacob¦14407 sent¦14406 for Rahel¦14409 and¦14406 Le'ah¦14410 to¦14410 \add come to him out in\add* the¦14411 countryside¦14411 \add where he was with\add* his¦14414 flocks¦14414
\v 5 and¦14416 he¦14416 told¦14416 them¦14417, “I've¦14419 \add noticed\add* your¦14423 father's \add attitude\add* and that¦14424 he's¦14426 not¦14426 \add positive\add* toward me¦14427 \add like he was a few days\add* ago¦14429, but¦14416 my father's god¦14430 has¦14432 been¦14432 with¦14433 me¦14433.
\v 6 You \add both\add* know¦14436 that¦14437 I've¦14441 served¦14441 your¦14444 father¦14444 with all¦14438 my¦14440 strength¦14440,
\v 7 \add but\add* your¦14446 father¦14446 has¦14447 deceived¦14447 me and¦14446 changed¦14449 my¦14452 wages¦14452 ten¦14453 times¦14454. However¦14450, God¦14458 hasn't allowed¦14457 him¦14457 to¦14459 harm¦14459 me¦14460.
\v 8 \add When he told me\add*: ‘The speckled¦14466 animals will¦14467 be¦14467 your¦14468 wages,’ then all the flocks bore speckled young. But¦14469 when he \add ≈told me\add*: ‘The streaked ones will¦14479 be¦14479 your¦14480 wages,’ then all¦14482 the¦14484 flocks¦14484 bore streaked young.
\v 9 \add In that way,\add* God¦14488 took¦14487 your¦14492 father's¦14492 animals¦14491 away¦14487 from him and¦14493 gave¦14493 them to¦14495 me¦14495.
\p
\v 10 “\add One day during\add* the season¦14498 when the flocks were¦14499 \add mating\add*, I¦14501 \add looked up\add* and¦14503 saw¦14503 in¦14498 a dream¦14504 that, wow, the¦14506 male¦14506 goats¦14506 that¦14507 were¦14507 mounting the¦14510 flocks¦14510 were¦14511 streaked¦14511, speckled¦14512, and¦14513 spotted.
\v 11 Then¦14515 God's messenger¦14517 said to¦14516 me¦14516 in¦14519 the¦14517 dream¦14519, ‘Yacob¦14520!’ and¦14515 I¦14521 said¦14521, ‘\add I'm listening\add*.’
\v 12 Then¦14524 he¦14524 \add ≈told¦14524 me\add*, ‘Please¦14527 \add look up\add* and¦14529 \add observe that\add* all¦14530 the¦14532 male¦14532 goats¦14532 that¦14533 are¦14533 mounting the¦14536 flocks¦14536 are¦14537 streaked¦14537, speckled¦14538, and¦14539 spotted, because¦14540 I¦14541 have¦14541 seen¦14541 everything that¦14545 Lavan¦14546 is¦14547 doing¦14547 to¦14548 you¦14548.
\v 13 I'm¦14550 the¦14551 god¦14551 of¦14552 Beyt¦14552-El¦14554, where¦14555 you¦14556 anointed¦14556 a pillar¦14558—where¦14559 you¦14560 vowed¦14560 a vow¦14563 to me¦14561. Now¦14564 \add pack\add* up and depart¦14566 from¦14567 this¦14570 land, and¦14571 return¦14571 to the land where you were¦14551 born.’ ”\x + \xo 31:13: \xt Gen 28:18-22.\x*
\p
\v 14 Then¦14577 Rahel¦14578 and¦14577 Le'ah¦14579 replied¦14580, “\add Yes,\add* we're not expecting any portion¦14584 or inheritance¦14585 from our¦14587 father's¦14587 \add property\add*.
\v 15 Doesn't he just \add treat\add* us like foreigners¦14590 \add now\add*? \add Yes,\add* he¦14594 sold¦14594 us¦14594 and¦14595 then he¦14595 \add frittered away all the money that should have been\add* ours,
\v 16 so all¦14604 the¦14606 wealth¦14606 that¦14607 God took¦14608 from¦14610 our father¦14610 \add belonged\add* to¦14611 us¦14611 and¦14613 to¦14613 our children¦14613 \add anyway\add*. So \add yes\add*, \add go ahead and\add* do¦14620 everything that God's¦14618 told¦14617 you¦14619 \add to do\add*.”
\p
\v 17 So¦14622 Yacob¦14623 \add packed\add* up¦14622 and¦14624 put his¦14627 wives¦14630 and children¦14627 on¦14631 the¦14633 camels¦14633.
\v 18 Then¦14635 he¦14635 drove¦14635 all his livestock and¦14635 all¦14638 his¦14640 property¦14645 that¦14646 he¦14647 had¦14647 acquired—the¦14648 livestock¦14648 in his¦14649 possession¦14649 that¦14650 he¦14651 had¦14651 acquired in¦14652 Paddan¦14652-Aram¦14653—to¦14654 go¦14654 \add back\add* to¦14655 Isaac¦14657 his¦14658 father¦14658 in the Canaan¦14660 region¦14659.
\v 19 \add Now\add* Lavan had¦14663 gone¦14663 \add off for several days\add* to¦14664 shear¦14664 his¦14667 sheep¦14667, so Rahel¦14669 stole¦14668 the¦14672 idols¦14672 that¦14673 belonged¦14674 to¦14674 her¦14674 father¦14674,
