\p
\v 1 Then Yacob \add continued on\add* his way \add with his family and flocks\add*, and \add some\add* of¦15305 God's messengers met him
\v 2 and¦15308 when he saw them, Yacob¦15308 said, “This \add must be\add* God's¦15315 army camp.” So he named that place ‘Mahanaim’ \add (which means ‘two camps’)\add*.
\s1 Yacob sends gifts ahead for Esaw
\rem /s1 Jacob Sends Presents to Appease Esau
\p
\v 3 Then Yacob¦15319 sent messengers ahead of him to his brother Esaw in the Se'ir region in the country of Edom,
\v 4 instructing them, “This is what you'll say to my master, to Esaw¦15340: ‘This is what your servant Yacob¦15335 says, “I have been staying with \add Uncle\add* Lavan and¦15334 have remained there until now.
\v 5 \add Now\add* I¦15363 have¦15362 cattle and donkeys, flocks, and male and female slaves. And¦15348 I've¦15362 sent \add these messengers\add* to¦15350 speak with¦15359 my¦15353 master¦15353, so¦15351 that I'll find favour in your¦15357 eyes.” ’ ”
\p
\v 6 \add In due course\add* the messengers returned to Yacob, saying, “We went to your¦15383 brother Esaw and¦15369 \add now\add* he's¦15369 coming to meet you along with¦15383 his four hundred men!”
\v 7 \add This made\add* Yacob¦15390 very scared and¦15399 distressed, so he¦15400 divided the people¦15405 who were¦15400 with¦15406 him¦15406 and the flocks and the herds and the camels into two groups,
\v 8 \add reasoning\add*, “If Esaw comes and¦15409 attacks one camp, then the¦15417 camp that's¦15418 left can escape.”
\p
\v 9 Then \add he prayed\add*, “Yahweh, God of my grandfather Abraham, and¦15432 God of my father Yitshak, who said¦15432 to me, ‘Return to your land and to your relatives, and I will¦15435 cause things to¦15437 prosper with you,’
\v 10 I'm unworthy of all the kindnesses and¦15448 of all the¦15453 faithfulness that¦15457 you¦15463 have shown \add me\add* your¦15460 slave, because I¦15462 crossed this Yordan \add River\add* with¦15463 \add only\add* my staff, but¦15448 now I've become two camps.
\v 11 Please save me from¦15467 my¦15478 brother Esaw, because¦15477 I'm¦15466 afraid that¦15472 he'll come and attack me and the mothers with¦15478 the children.
\v 12 But¦15504 you said,\x + \xo 32:12: \xt Gen 22:17.\x* ‘I¦15499 will¦15504 surely cause things to prosper with¦15506 you, and¦15504 I'll make your descendants¦15508 as \add numerous as\add* the sand \add grains on the beach\add* which are too many to be counted.’ ”
\p
\v 13 Then he stayed there for that¦15522 night and¦15511 he \add selected\add* gifts for his brother Esaw from¦15526 what he had¦15512 with¦15515 him:
\v 14 two hundred female and¦15529 twenty male goats, two hundred ewes and¦15533 twenty rams,
\v 15 thirty milk camels with their young, forty cows and ten bulls, and¦15549 twenty¦15550 female¦15543 and ten male¦15545 donkeys.
\v 16 Then he \add handed them over\add* to his slaves, each herd by itself, and¦15555 he \add ≈told them\add*, “Go ahead of¦15555 me \add one by one\add*, and \add keep a\add* space between each herd.”
\v 17 And¦15568 he¦15568 instructed the¦15569 first one, saying¦15575, “When Esaw my¦15580 brother meets you and asks¦15575 you, saying, ‘Who do you belong to, and where are¦15574 you going? And¦15575 who do those animals belong to?’
\v 18 then you¦15595 \add should answer\add*, ‘They belong¦15602 to your¦15609 servant Yacob. They are¦15606 a gift sent to my¦15598 master Esaw¦15597. \add In fact, he's coming along\add* behind us.’ ”
\v 19 Then \add Yacob\add* also¦15612 instructed the second and¦15612 third slaves, as well as everyone who followed behind¦15624 the herds, \add telling them\add*, “Say¦15612 the same thing to¦15613 Esaw¦15619 when you¦15612 find him,
\v 20 and also¦15627 say¦15644, ‘Look, your servant Yacob is¦15641 behind¦15642 us.’ ” \add Yacob was thinking\add*, “I'll \add cheer him up\add* with¦15651 the¦15631 gifts that are¦15641 going¦15641 ahead of¦15639 me, and after that, when¦15651 I see \add him in person\add*, perhaps he'll \add accept me\add*.”
\v 21 \add So\add* the gifts¦15666 went¦15667 ahead¦15668 of¦15658 him, and¦15669 he¦15675 himself stayed in¦15666 the camp for¦15661 that¦15667 night.
\s1 Yacob gets renamed after fighting at Penu'el
\rem /s1 Jacob Wrestles With God; Jacob Wrestles with God; Jacob Wrestles at Peniel
\p
\v 22 Then during¦15686 that¦15688 night¦15685, \add Yacob\add* got up and took his two wives and \add their\add* two female slaves and his eleven sons and crossed¦15679 over the ford of the Yabbok \add Stream\add*.
\v 23 \add After\add* crossing¦15710 the¦15699 stream, he¦15710 \add also\add* sent across¦15710 \add everything else that\add* belonged to him.
\v 24 Then Yacob was left alone, and¦15716 a man wrestled with him¦15726 until dawn.\x + \xo 32:24-26: \xt Hos 12:3-4.\x*
\v 25 \add When the man realised\add* he wasn't gaining on him¦15735, he touched \add Yacob\add* on the socket of his hip so that it¦15732 became dislocated as \add they\add* wrestled¦15733 with¦15735 \add each other\add*.
\v 26 Then \add the man\add* said, “Release me \add now\add*, because¦15742 it's¦15750 \add already\add* dawning.”
\p “I won't¦15743 release you until you bless me,” Yacob¦15754 \add ≈responded\add*.
\p
\v 27 “What's your name?” the¦15763 man \add asked\add*.
\p “Yacob,” he¦15764 \add ≈replied¦15759\add*.
\p
\v 28 “You won't be¦15777 called¦15777 Yacob¦15779 anymore,” the man said¦15773, “but¦15773 \add you'll be\add* ‘Yisra'el’ \add !(‘Israel’,\add* \add which means ‘he struggled with God’)\add*, because you have struggled with God and with men, and you won.”\x + \xo 32:28: \xt Gen 35:10.\x*
\p
\v 29 “Please tell¦15782 \add me\add* \em your¦15787\em* name¦15787,” Yacob¦15784 \add requested\add*.\x + \xo 32:29: \xt Jdg 13:17-18.\x*
\p “Why \add would you want to know\add* my name?” \add the man replied\add*, then he¦15782 blessed Yacob there.
\p
\v 30 \add So\add* Yacob¦15805 named the place ‘Penu'el’ \add (also spelt ‘Peni'el’, which means ‘God's face’)\add*, because he¦15804 said¦15806, “I saw God face to¦15812 face, yet my¦15815 life was preserved.”
\v 31 And¦15821 the¦15823 sun rose above him as he passed through Penu'el, and¦15834 he was¦15834 limping because¦15826 of¦15823 his hip.
\v 32 That's why Israelis don't eat the muscle of the tendon that is¦15848 on the hip socket to¦15840 this day, because \add the man\add* touched the¦15841 socket of Yacob's hip on¦15849 the muscle of¦15851 the tendon.
\c 33
\s1 Esaw and Yacob meet peacefully
\rem /s1 Jacob and Esau Meet; Jacob Meets Esau; Jacob and Esau Make Peace
\p
\v 1 Then Yacob¦15885 \add raised his head\add* and¦15887 looked¦15887 \add ahead\add*, and¦15888 wow, Esaw¦15889 was¦15890 coming¦15890 \add towards him\add* along with¦15899 \add his\add* four¦15892 hundred¦15893 men¦15894. Then \add Yacob quickly\add* divided¦15895 the¦15898 children¦15898 among Le'ah¦15901 and¦15902 Rahel¦15904 and¦15905 \add their\add* two¦15906 female slaves¦15907,
\v 2 and¦15909 he¦15909 put¦15909 the¦15912 slave¦15912 women and¦15913 their¦15915 children first¦15916, and then¦15909 Le'ah¦15919 and¦15920 her¦15920 children after them, and¦15922 \add finally\add* Rahel¦15924 and¦15925 Yosef¦15927 after them.
\v 3 Then¦15930 he himself went¦15939 ahead¦15932 of them¦15932, and¦15930 he bowed¦15933 to¦15940 the ground¦15934 seven¦15935 times¦15936 as he¦15939 approached¦15939 his¦15942 brother¦15942.
\v 4 \add But\add* Esaw¦15945 ran¦15944 \add forward\add* to¦15946 meet¦15946 him¦15946 and¦15947 embraced¦15947 him¦15947 and¦15948 \add threw his arms around\add* his neck¦15951 and¦15953 kissed¦15953 him¦15953, and¦15955 they¦15955 \add both\add* cried¦15955 \add together\add*.
\v 5 Then¦15957 \add Esaw looked up\add* and¦15961 saw¦15961 the¦15964 women¦15964 and¦15965 the¦15967 children, and¦15968 \add asked\add*, “Who¦15969 are¦15971 these¦15971 \add others\add* with you¦15972?”
\p “The¦15974 children that¦15969 God¦15978 has¦15977 graciously given to¦15977 your¦15981 servant¦15981,” Yacob replied¦15968.
\v 6 Then¦15983 the¦15984 \add two\add* female slaves¦15984 approached¦15983 with their¦15986 children¦15986, and¦15983 they¦15985 bowed¦15987 down¦15987.
\v 7 \add Next\add* Le'ah¦15992 also¦15993 approached with her¦15993 children¦15993, and they bowed down. Then¦15989 after¦15995 that, Yosef¦15997 and¦15998 Rahel¦15998 approached, and¦15999 they¦15999 bowed¦15999 down¦15999.
\p
\v 8 Then¦16001 \add Esaw asked\add*, “What were¦16004 all¦16004 these groups that¦16008 I¦16009 met¦16009?”
\p “To¦16011 \add win\add* my¦16015 master's¦16015 favour¦16013,” Yacob \add ≈replied¦16001\add*.
\p
\v 9 “I've got plenty, my¦16023 brother¦16023,” said¦16017 Esaw¦16018. “\add Keep\add* what belongs¦16024 to¦16021 you.”
\p
\v 10 “No¦16032, please¦16034,” Yacob¦16031 \add insisted\add*. “If¦16035 I've \add won\add* your¦16040 favour¦16039, then¦16030 take¦16053 my¦16042 gifts¦16042. Because¦16044 indeed, I've seen¦16048 you face-to-face, which is like¦16050 seeing¦16050 God's¦16051 face, and¦16030 you've¦16053 received¦16053 me¦16053 \add favourably\add*.
\v 11 Please¦16057 take¦16055 my¦16060 \add gifts\add* that¦16061 were¦16062 brought¦16062 to¦16063 you, because¦16068 God¦16067 has¦16066 been¦16062 gracious¦16066 to¦16066 me¦16066 and¦16068 I have¦16066 \add way more than I need\add*.”
\p And¦16074 he¦16074 urged¦16074 him¦16076, so \add Esaw\add* took¦16077 it¦16076
\v 12 and¦16079 said¦16079, “\add Okay,\add* let's¦16080 get moving and¦16081 go¦16081, and¦16082 I'll¦16082 go¦16082 ahead¦16083 of you¦16083.”
\p
\v 13 But¦16085 \add Yacob replied\add*, “My¦16087 master¦16087 knows¦16088 that¦16089 the¦16091 children¦16091 are¦16092 tender plus¦16093 I have flocks and¦16085 herds¦16094 \add with young animals\add*. If¦16089 they¦16097 drive¦16097 them¦16097 \add harder today\add*, then¦16085 all¦16101 the flocks will¦16092 die¦16100.
\v 14 Please¦16107 let¦16105 my master go¦16105 on¦16105 before¦16109 his¦16110 servant¦16110, and¦16111 I'll¦16112 lead them on¦16112 at my¦16114 gentle¦16114 pace—at the¦16115 pace of¦16115 the¦16116 livestock¦16116 that¦16117 are ahead of me and¦16120 at the¦16120 pace of¦16120 the¦16121 children¦16121—until¦16122 I¦16111 come¦16125 to¦16126 my¦16128 master's¦16128 \add place\add* in¦16109 Se'ir.”
\p
\v 15 “\add At least\add* let¦16133 me¦16133 leave some¦16137 of¦16137 my¦16149 men¦16139 with¦16141 you¦16136 \add all\add*,” said¦16131 Esaw¦16132.
\p “Why do that¦16140?” \add contradicted Yacob\add*. “May my master¦16149 \add allow me to decide\add*.”
\v 16 \add So\add* Esaw¦16154 \add and his men\add* started heading \add home\add* to¦16156 Se'ir¦16156,
\v 17 \add but\add* Yacob travelled to¦16162 Succot \add where he\add* built¦16161 a house¦16163 for himself and¦16158 made¦16165 shelters¦16166 for his¦16164 livestock¦16164. That's why he named¦16171 the¦16171 place¦16173 ‘Succot’ \add (which means ‘shelters’)\add*.
\s1 Yacob begins to settle at Shekem
\rem /s1 Jacob Reaches Shechem
\p
\v 18 Then Yacob¦16178, having come from¦16186 Paddan¦16186-Aram, arrived¦16177 peacefully at¦16185 the city of¦16180 Shekem¦16181 in¦16185 the Canaan¦16184 region¦16183, and¦16188 he¦16188 camped¦16188 \add outside\add* the city¦16192.
\v 19 \add In due course,\add* he¦16194 bought¦16194 the¦16197 portion¦16197 of¦16197 the¦16198 field¦16198 where¦16199 he'd pitched¦16200 his¦16203 tents¦16203 from¦16204 the sons¦16205 of¦16205 Hamor¦16207, the¦16208 father¦16208 of¦16208 Shekem¦16209, for¦16210 a hundred¦16210 \add pieces of silver\add*.\x + \xo 33:19: \xt Josh 24:32; Yhn 4:5.\x*
\v 20 He¦16213 set¦16213 up¦16213 an¦16216 altar¦16216 there¦16215 and¦16213 he¦16213 named¦16217 it¦16217 ‘El¦16220 Elohe¦16221 Yisra'el¦16222’ \add (which means ‘God, the god of Yisra'el’)\add*.
\c 34
\s1 Dinah's rape leads to a plan
\rem /s1 The Rape of Dinah; Dinah and the Shechemites; Revenge against Shechem
\p
\v 1 \add One day,\add* Yacob¦16232 and¦16225 Le'ah's¦16229 daughter¦16227 Dinah¦16226, went¦16225 out¦16225 to¦16232 \add visit some of\add* the¦16235 \add local women\add*,
\v 2 \add but\add* Shekem¦16239, the¦16240 son¦16240 of¦16240 Hamor¦16242 the¦16243 Hivite¦16243, the¦16244 ruler of¦16244 the¦16245 land¦16245, saw¦16237 her and he¦16248 \add grabbed\add* her¦16249 and¦16250 \add raped\add* her¦16250.
\v 3 \add Shekem admired Dinah so much that he fell in love with her\add* and¦16252 spoke¦16262 \add sweetly to her to try to cultivate a relationship\add*.
\v 4 Then¦16268 \add he asked\add* Hamor¦16272 his¦16273 father¦16273, “Get¦16269 this¦16281 girl¦16280 for¦16282 me¦16277 as a wife¦16282.”
\p
\v 5 \add When\add* Yacob heard¦16285 that¦16286 \add Shekem\add* had¦16287 dishonoured his daughter¦16291 Dinah¦16290, his¦16291 sons¦16292 were¦16293 \add out\add* in¦16297 the¦16297 countryside¦16297 with¦16294 his livestock¦16296, so Yacob \add waited quietly\add* until¦16300 they¦16302 \add got home\add*.
\v 6 \add Meanwhile\add* Shekem's¦16308 father¦16306 Hamor¦16305 \add took Shekem\add* to¦16309 \add negotiate\add* with¦16313 Yacob¦16311.
\v 7 \add In due course\add* Yacob's sons¦16315 came¦16317 \add home\add* from¦16318 the¦16320 countryside¦16320. When¦16315 they heard¦16321 \add what had happened\add*, then¦16315 they¦16323 were¦16322 \add very angry and upset\add*, because¦16327 \add Shekem\add* had¦16330 done¦16330 something disgraceful¦16329 to¦16325 Yisra'el¦16331 by¦16332 \add taking advantage of\add* Yacob's daughter¦16335. \add Something like that should never have happened\add*.
\v 8 \add But\add* Hamor¦16343 spoke¦16342 with¦16344 them¦16344, saying¦16345, “My¦16347 son Shekem¦16346 my¦16347 son \add is madly in love with\add* your¦16350 daughter¦16350. Please¦16352 give¦16351 her¦16353 to¦16354 him¦16354 as a wife¦16355.
\v 9 \add In fact, why don't you allow us to marry\add* your daughters, and¦16357 you \add people could have\add* our¦16365 daughters \add to marry\add*,
\v 10 then¦16369 you could settle \add here permanently\add* with¦16369 us¦16369. \add This region would open up to you all so\add* settle in¦16377 it¦16372 and¦16375 trade¦16375 \add with us\add* and¦16376 \add you could\add* buy \add more land around here\add*.”
\p
\v 11 Then¦16379 Shekem¦16380 spoke¦16379 to¦16381 \add Dinah's\add* father¦16383 and¦16385 brothers¦16387, “\add Look kindly on my request\add* and¦16392 I'll¦16395 give¦16395 \add whatever you ask for\add*.
\v 12 \add Set any very high amount for\add* the bride-price¦16400 and¦16401 gifts¦16401 \add from\add* me, and¦16402 I'll¦16402 give¦16402 \add whatever you ask\add*—\add just\add* give¦16406 the¦16411 young woman¦16412 to¦16412 me as¦16403 a wife¦16412.”
\p
\v 13 \add But because\add* Shekem had¦16428 \add abused\add* their¦16431 sister¦16431 Dinah¦16430, Yacob's¦16417 sons¦16415 \add gave a false answer\add* to Shekem and¦16414 his¦16424 father¦16424,
\v 14 \add stating\add*, “\add Sorry,\add* we¦16436 can't¦16435 do¦16437 that¦16439 because¦16449 it¦16447 would be¦16451 a disgrace¦16451 \add in our culture\add* to allow a man¦16444 with a foreskin¦16448 \add to marry her\add*.
\v 15 We'd only¦16455 consent \add to your proposal\add* if¦16460 you'd become like¦16462 us¦16462 by¦16463 circumcising¦16463 every¦16465 male¦16467 among you,
\v 16 Then¦16469 we'd give¦16469 our¦16472 daughters to¦16473 you \add to marry\add*, and¦16474 we'd take¦16477 your daughters for¦16479 us¦16479 \add to marry\add*. And¦16480 we'd settle¦16480 among you, and¦16482 we¦16482 \add all\add* would¦16482 become¦16482 one¦16484 \add united\add* people¦16483.
\v 17 \add But\add* if¦16486 you¦16489 all won't¦16488 \add agree\add* to¦16490 get¦16492 circumcised¦16491, then¦16486 we'll¦16492 \add just\add* take¦16492 \add Dinah\add* and¦16486 go¦16496.”
\p
\v 18 \add This idea\add* pleased¦16498 Hamor¦16501 and¦16502 his son¦16504,
\v 19 \add so Shekem\add* didn't¦16508 delay¦16510 \add implementing the plan\add* because¦16514 he was the most honoured¦16520 son in¦16516 his¦16523 father's¦16523 household¦16522, and¦16508 he was so delighted¦16515 with¦16516 Yacob's¦16518 daughter¦16516.
\p
\v 20 So¦16525 Hamor¦16526 and¦16527 Shekem¦16527 went¦16525 to¦16529 \add the city elders at\add* the¦16531 gate¦16531 of¦16536 their city, and they¦16533 spoke¦16533 to them, saying¦16538,
\v 21 “These¦16541 men¦16540 are¦16542 peaceful¦16542 towards us¦16544, so let¦16545 them¦16545 settle¦16545 in¦16546 the¦16546 land, and¦16547 let¦16547 them¦16547 trade¦16547 in¦16547 it¦16548. And¦16549 look, the¦16549 land \add is plenty wide enough for them as well\add*. We¦16550 can take¦16558 their¦16557 daughters for¦16560 ourselves as wives¦16561, and¦16562 we¦16565 can give¦16565 our¦16564 daughters to¦16566 them¦16566 \add to marry\add*.
\v 22 \add But\add* they'll¦16571 only¦16568 consent to settle¦16574 among us and unite with¦16570 us on¦16570 this¦16570 \add condition\add*: we would¦16571 need to circumcise¦16579 all¦16581 of¦16581 the¦16573 males¦16583 amongst us, just¦16584 like¦16584 they're¦16585 circumcised¦16586.
\v 23 Won't all of¦16588 their livestock¦16588 and their property¦16589 and¦16590 all¦16590 their animals¦16592 then belong to¦16594 us¦16594? \add So\add* let's¦16597 agree¦16597 with¦16600 \add their condition\add* and then they'll¦16599 settle¦16599 among¦16600 us¦16600.”
\v 24 All¦16610 \add the elders\add* at the city gate \add agreed with\add* Hamor¦16605 and¦16606 his¦16609 son¦16609 Shekem¦16608, and¦16615 \add so\add* every¦16616 male¦16618 who¦16612 \add passed through\add* the¦16613 city gate was¦16615 circumcised¦16615.
\rem /s1 Dinah's Brothers Avenge Their Sister
\p
\v 25 Three days¦16626 later when \add all those men\add* were in¦16626 pain¦16629 \add from the cutting\add*, two¦16631 of¦16633 Yacob's¦16635 sons¦16633, Simeon¦16636 and¦16637 Levi¦16637 who were Dinah's¦16639 brothers¦16638, took¦16630 their¦16628 swords¦16641 and¦16642 boldly attacked the¦16645 city¦16645 and¦16647 slaughtered¦16647 every¦16648 male¦16650,
\v 26 including¦16655 Hamor¦16654 and¦16655 his¦16658 son¦16658 Shekem¦16668. Then¦16652 they¦16659 retrieved Dinah¦16666 from¦16667 Shekem's¦16657 house¦16667 and¦16669 left¦16669 \add the city\add*.
\v 27 Then when Yacob's¦16672 \add other sons\add* discovered that¦16679 a slaughter \add had taken place\add*, they¦16673 looted¦16677 the¦16676 city¦16678 because their¦16681 sister¦16681 had¦16680 been violated—
\v 28 taking¦16701 flocks¦16685 and¦16686 herds¦16688 and¦16689 donkeys¦16691—anything the was¦16696 in¦16696 the city¦16696 or \add out\add* in¦16700 the¦16700 countryside¦16700.
\v 29 They¦16716 captured¦16716 their women¦16715 and children and took¦16716 all¦16710 their wealth¦16707 and everything that¦16721 was¦16722 in¦16722 their houses¦16722.
\p
\v 30 \add Afterwards,\add* Yacob¦16725 scolded Simeon¦16728 and¦16729 Levi¦16731, saying¦16724, “You \add two\add* have¦16732 \add made\add* trouble¦16732 for me¦16733 by¦16734 \add destroying my reputation with\add* those who live in¦16735 the land¦16736—the Canaanites¦16737 and¦16738 the Perizzites¦16738. \add There's only a few of us\add*, and if they¦16742 gather¦16742 together to¦16726 attack¦16744 me \add and my household\add*, then¦16724 \add we'll\add* be¦16745 destroyed¦16745—me and¦16747 \add all\add* my household¦16747.”
\p
\v 31 \add But\add* they¦16749 \add ≈responded¦16749\add*, “Should he¦16751 \add have gotten away with\add* treating our¦16754 sister¦16754 like¦16750 a prostitute¦16750?”
\c 35
\s1 God blesses Yacob at Beyt-El
\rem /s1 Jacob Returns to Bethel; Jacob's Return to Bethel; God Blesses Jacob at Bethel
\p
\v 1 Then God¦16758 told¦16757 Yacob¦16761, “\add Pack\add* up¦16763 and \add move\add* to Beyt¦16764-El¦16766 and¦16767 settle¦16767 there¦16769, and¦16770 make¦16770 an¦16773 altar¦16773 there to¦16774 the god¦16774 who¦16775 appeared¦16775 to¦16776 you¦16776 when¦16777 you were fleeing¦16777 from¦16779 your brother¦16781 Esaw¦16780.”\x + \xo 35:1: \xt Gen 28:11-17.\x*
\p
\v 2 \add So\add* Yacob¦16784 instructed his¦16787 household¦16787 and¦16788 \add everyone\add* with¦16799 him¦16792, “Remove¦16794 \add any\add* foreign¦16797 \add idols\add* that¦16798 are¦16799 among¦16799 you¦16799, and¦16800 purify¦16800 yourselves¦16800 and¦16801 change¦16801 your¦16802 clothes¦16802.
\v 3 Then¦16804 \add we'll leave here\add* and¦16805 \add make the uphill trip\add* to Beyt¦16806-El¦16808, and¦16809 I'll¦16809 make¦16809 an¦16812 altar¦16812 there¦16811 to¦16813 God¦16813, who¦16814 answered¦16814 me¦16815 \add when I was\add* distressed¦16817. He's¦16818 been¦16818 with¦16820 me \add wherever\add* I've¦16822 gone¦16822.”
\v 4 So¦16824 they¦16824 gave¦16824 Yacob¦16827 all¦16829 \add their idols and their earrings\add*, and \add he buried\add* them¦16841 under¦16843 the¦16844 terebinth¦16844 tree¦16844 that¦16833 was¦16846 near¦16846 Shekem¦16848.
\p
\v 5 Then¦16850 they \add started their journey but\add* and¦16850 the¦16853 \add people of\add* the¦16857 cities¦16857 around¦16859 them¦16859 \add were afraid of Yacob's god\add* so they didn't¦16860 \add attack them\add*.
\v 6 \add So\add* Yacob¦16867 and¦16866 everyone¦16879 with¦16882 him¦16882 \add eventually arrived\add* at Luz¦16868 in¦16870 the¦16879 Canaan¦16871 region¦16870 (which¦16880 is¦16873 \add now named\add* Beyt¦16873-El¦16875).
\v 7 He¦16884 built¦16884 an¦16886 altar¦16886 there and¦16884 named¦16887 the place¦16888 ‘El¦16889 Beyt¦16890-El¦16892’ \add (which means ‘the god of Beyt-El’)\add*, because¦16893 God had¦16895 revealed¦16895 himself to¦16896 him¦16896 there when¦16898 he¦16898 was fleeing¦16898 from¦16899 his¦16900 brother¦16900 \add Esaw\add*.
\v 8 Then¦16902 Rebekah's¦16905 nurse¦16904 Deborah¦16903 died¦16902 and¦16902 was¦16906 buried¦16906 under¦16907 the oak tree below Beyt¦16908-El¦16910 \add so\add* he¦16913 named¦16914 \add the place\add* ‘Allon Bakut’ \add (which means ‘oak of weeping’)\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add Now that Yacob had left\add* Paddan¦16926-Aram and \add come back to Beyt-El\add*, God¦16920 appeared¦16919 to¦16921 him \add there\add* again¦16924 and¦16928 blessed¦16928 him¦16929
\v 10 and¦16931 told¦16931 him¦16933, “Your¦16940 name¦16935 is¦16936 Yacob \add but\add* you won't¦16937 be called Yacob anymore. \add From now on,\add* you'll be called Yisra'el (‘Israel¦16947’).” So¦16931 \add again\add*\x + \xo 35:10: \xt Gen 32:28.\x* \add God\add* called \add him\add* Yisra'el¦16954.
\v 11 Then¦16956 God \add also told\add* him¦16957, “I'm¦16959 God¦16960 the provider. Be¦16962 fruitful¦16962 and¦16963 multiply¦16963. Out¦16971 of you¦16968 will come a nation¦16964 and¦16965 a community of¦16965 nations¦16966, and¦16969 kings¦16969 will come from¦16968 your¦16970 \add descendants\add*,\x + \xo 35:11-12: \xt Gen 17:4-8.\x*
\v 12 and¦16973 I'll give you the¦16975 land¦16975 that¦16976 I¦16981 gave¦16977 to¦16978 Abraham¦16978 and¦16979 to¦16979 Isaac¦16979, and \add in the future,\add* I'll give the land to¦16982 your¦16982 descendants¦16982 after¦16983 you¦16983.”
\v 13 After God¦16991 finished talking¦16995 to Yacob, he¦16995 left him¦16990 and¦16989 went \add back\add* up.
\v 14 Then¦16998 Yacob¦16999 set¦16998 up¦16998 a stone¦17007 pillar¦17000 at¦17001 the place¦17001 where¦17002 \add God\add* had¦17004 spoken¦17004 with¦17001 him¦17005, and¦16998 he¦17004 poured¦17008 a drink¦17010 offering¦17010 over it¦17005, followed by oil¦17013,\x + \xo 35:14-15: \xt Gen 28:18-19.\x*
\v 15 and¦17015 he¦17015 named¦17019 that place¦17020 ‘Beyt¦17026-El’ \add (which means ‘God's house’) because\add* God¦17025 had¦17022 spoken¦17022 to him¦17023 there¦17024.
\s1 Rahel dies giving birth to Benyamin
\rem /s1 The Birth of Benjamin and the Death of Rachel; The Death of Rachel; The Deaths of Rachel and Isaac
\p
\v 16 Then they¦17030 moved on¦17044 from¦17031 Beyt¦17031-El, and¦17030 there was still quite a distance¦17036 to¦17039 go¦17039 to reach to \add the town of\add* Efrath¦17040. Then Rahel¦17042 \add went into labour\add*, but¦17030 was having¦17043 great difficulty¦17043 in¦17044 \add delivering the baby\add*.
\v 17 \add At one point\add* when¦17047 she¦17047 was¦17046 in¦17047 hard labour¦17048, the¦17051 midwife¦17051 said¦17049 to¦17060 her¦17048, “Don't¦17052 be¦17054 afraid¦17054. You've got another son¦17061.”
\v 18 \add But Rahel\add* was dying¦17067, and¦17063 as her \add spirit\add* was leaving her¦17065, she¦17067 named¦17068 \add the baby\add* ‘Ben'oni’ \add (which means ‘son of my sorrow’)\add*, but¦17063 \add afterwards Yacob\add* renamed him¦17076 ‘Benyamin¦17077’ \add (which means ‘son of my right hand’)\add*.
\p
\v 19 \add Thus\add* Rahel¦17080 died¦17079 and¦17081 was¦17081 buried¦17081 on¦17082 the¦17082 path¦17082 to Efrath¦17083 (which¦17084 is¦17085 \add now called\add* Bethlehem).
\v 20 Yacob¦17089 set¦17088 up¦17088 a¦17090 \add stone\add* pillar¦17090 over¦17091 her¦17093 grave—that's the¦17095 pillar¦17095 of¦17095 Rahel's¦17098 grave to this day¦17101.
\v 21 Then¦17103 Yisra'el¦17104 \add and his household moved on\add* and¦17105 pitched¦17105 \add their\add* tents¦17106 beyond¦17108 Migdal Eder¦17111.
\s1 Yisra'el's sons
