\p
\v 22 While they¦17133 were¦17133 living¦17114 in¦17114 that¦17117 area, \add Yisra'el's son\add* Reuben¦17119 slept with¦17114 his¦17127 father's¦17127 slave-wife Bilhah¦17124, and¦17113 Yisra'el¦17115 found out \add about it\add*.\x + \xo 35:22: \xt Gen 49:4.\x*
\p \add Yisra'el\add* now had twelve sons¦17134.
\v 23 Le'ah's¦17141 sons¦17140 were his eldest¦17142 son¦17140 Reuven¦17144, and¦17145 then to Simeon¦17145, Levi¦17146, Yihudah¦17147, Yissakar¦17148, and¦17149 Zebulun¦17149.
\v 24 Rahel's¦17152 sons¦17151 were Yosef¦17153 and¦17154 Benyamin¦17154.
\v 25 The¦17156 sons¦17156 of¦17157 Rahel's¦17159 slave¦17158 woman Bilhah¦17157 were Dan¦17160 and¦17161 Naftali¦17161.
\v 26 The¦17163 sons¦17163 of¦17164 Leah's¦17166 slave¦17165 women Zilpah¦17164 were Gad¦17167 and¦17163 Asher¦17168. Those were¦17170 \add Yisra'el's\add* sons¦17170 who¦17172 were¦17173 \add nearly all\add* born¦17173 in¦17176 Paddan¦17176-Aram¦17177.
\s1 Yitshak's death
