\c 37
\s1 Yosef's dreams cause conflict
\rem /s1 Joseph; Joseph Dreams of Greatness; Joseph's Dreams; Joseph and His Brothers
\p
\v 1 Yisra'el¦17819 \add !(Israel¦17819/Yacob¦17819/Jacob¦17819)\add* lived¦17818 in¦17820 the¦17821 area where his¦17822 father¦17822 \add Yitshak\add* had stayed, in¦17823 the Canaan¦17824 region¦17820.
\v 2 This is¦17828 \add the record of his\add* descendants¦17831:
\p When¦17830 Yosef \add !(Joseph¦17830)\add* was¦17831 seventeen¦17833, he¦17837 was¦17837 shepherding¦17838 the flocks¦17842 with¦17842 his brothers¦17841. He¦17843 was \add younger than his brothers\add* who were the sons¦17831 of his father's¦17854 \add slave\add* wives¦17853 Bilhah¦17848 and¦17855 Zilpah¦17852. \add One day\add* Yosef¦17856 gave a \add tell-tale\add* bad¦17860 report¦17859 about¦17828 them to¦17861 their¦17863 father.
\p
\v 3 \add Now\add* Yisra'el¦17865 loved¦17866 Yosef¦17869 more than¦17870 all¦17870 of¦17872 his¦17872 \add other\add* sons¦17872 because¦17873 he was¦17875 \add born to him when he was already old\add*, so he made¦17880 a multicoloured robe¦17882 for him.
\v 4 \add When\add* his brothers saw¦17885 that¦17887 their¦17891 father¦17891 loved¦17890 \add Yosef\add* more than¦17892 all¦17892 of¦17894 his¦17894 brothers, they¦17895 hated¦17895 him and¦17885 couldn't \add make themselves say anything nice\add* to¦17900 him.
\p
\v 5 \add One night\add* Yosef¦17903 had a dream¦17904, and¦17902 he¦17902 told¦17905 his¦17906 brothers¦17906 about¦17906 it¦17910, \add but\add* that made them hate¦17909 him¦17910 even more.
\v 6 He¦17912 \add ≈told¦17912\add* them¦17913, “Please¦17916 \add listen about\add* this¦17918 dream¦17917 that¦17919 I¦17920 \add had\add*:
\v 7 See¦17922, we¦17923 were¦17924 \add tying up bundles of grain stalks\add* in¦17926 the¦17926 middle¦17926 of a field¦17927, and¦17928 wow, my¦17930 bundle got up and¦17931 stood¦17933 upright¦17933. Then¦17922 \add would you believe it\add*, your bundles gathered¦17935 around¦17935 and¦17937 bowed¦17937 down¦17937 to¦17938 my¦17938 \add one\add*.”
\p
\v 8 “Will¦17944 you¦17944 really reign¦17944 over us?” his brothers¦17942 \add retorted\add*. “\add Do you think\add* you'll really rule¦17948 over¦17950 us¦17950?” \add So\add* they¦17951 continued¦17940 to¦17953 hate¦17953 him¦17954 even more because of his¦17957 dreams¦17957 and¦17940 because of \add what he said\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then¦17962 \add Yosef had\add* another dream, and¦17966 \add again\add* he¦17966 told¦17969 his¦17968 brothers¦17968, “Listen, I¦17971 \add had\add* another dream¦17972, and¦17974 wow, the¦17975 sun¦17975 and¦17976 the¦17976 moon¦17976 and¦17977 eleven stars¦17979 were¦17980 bowing¦17980 down¦17980 to¦17981 me¦17981.”
\p
\v 10 \add When\add* he¦17983 told¦17994 his father and his brothers, his father scolded¦17990 him¦17995, “What's¦17996 this¦17998 dream¦17997 that¦17999 you¦18000 \add had\add*? Will¦18002 your mother¦18004 and I¦18003 and your brothers \add actually\add* come¦18001 to¦18006 bow¦18006 down¦18006 to¦18007 the¦18008 ground¦18008 to¦18008 you?”
\v 11 \add Consequently\add* his brothers¦18013 envied¦18010 him¦18012, but¦18010 his¦18013 father¦18014 \add kept pondering it\add*.\x + \xo 37:11: \xt Acts 7:9.\x*
\s1 Yosef is sold by his brothers
\rem /s1 Joseph Is Sold and Taken to Egypt; Joseph Is Sold by His Brothers; Joseph Sold by His Brothers
\p
\v 12 \add Sometime after that, Yosef's\add* brothers¦18021 went¦18020 to¦18022 shepherd their¦18027 father's¦18027 flocks¦18025 near Shekem¦18028.
\v 13 \add One day,\add* Yisra'el¦18031 said¦18030 to¦18032 Yosef¦18034, “Aren't your¦18036 brothers¦18036 \add away\add* shepherding near Shekem¦18038? Come¦18039 \add we'll get some supplies\add* and¦18030 I'll¦18040 send¦18040 you¦18040 to¦18041 them¦18041.”
\p “\add Sure\add*,” Yosef \add ≈replied¦18030\add*.
\p
\v 14 Then¦18046 he¦18046 \add ≈told¦18046\add* him¦18062, “Please¦18050 go¦18048 and see¦18051 \add how\add* your¦18055 brothers¦18055 \add are doing\add* and the¦18063 flocks¦18059 \add as well\add*, then¦18046 \add come and let me know\add*.”
\p So¦18046 he¦18062 sent¦18062 \add Yosef off\add* from¦18063 the Hebron¦18064 valley¦18063, and¦18060 he¦18065 went¦18065 to¦18066 Shekem¦18066.
\v 15 \add When he got there,\add* a man¦18069 \add noticed\add* him wandering¦18071 around the¦18074 countryside¦18072 and¦18068 asked¦18073 him, “What¦18070 are¦18078 you¦18078 looking¦18078 for¦18078?”
\p
\v 16 “I'm¦18084 looking¦18085 for¦18085 my¦18083 brothers¦18083,” he¦18080 answered¦18080. “Please¦18088 tell¦18086 me¦18089 where¦18090 they're \add looking after our flocks\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “They've¦18108 left¦18096 here¦18097,” the¦18095 man¦18095 responded¦18094. “I¦18099 heard¦18099 them¦18099 say¦18100, ‘Let's¦18101 go¦18101 to¦18102 Dothan¦18102.’ ”
\rem /s1 Joseph Sold into Slavery
\p So¦18094 Yosef¦18104 continued¦18094 on¦18108 after¦18105 his¦18106 brothers¦18106 and¦18094 found¦18107 them¦18107 at¦18108 Dotan¦18102,
\v 18 \add but\add* they¦18110 saw¦18110 him¦18111 from¦18112 a distance¦18112 and¦18110 before¦18113 he¦18114 \add got close\add* to¦18115 them¦18115, they¦18116 \add made plans among themselves\add* to¦18118 kill¦18118 him¦18118.
\v 19 “Look¦18125, that¦18128 master¦18126 \add dreamer\add* is¦18129 coming¦18129,” they¦18120 said¦18120 to¦18122 each¦18121 other.
\v 20 “\add Here's our chance to\add* kill¦18134 him and¦18131 throw¦18135 \add his body\add* into¦18136 one¦18136 of¦18136 the¦18137 pits¦18137 \add around here\add*. We'll say¦18138 that a \add wild\add* animal¦18139 \add attacked\add* him. \em Then¦18131\em* we'll¦18138 see¦18142 what¦18143 his¦18146 dreams¦18146 \add turn into\add*.”
\p
\v 21 But¦18148 Reuben¦18149 heard¦18148 \add what they were saying\add*, and¦18148 he¦18150 \add tried to\add* rescue¦18150 \add Yosef by insisting\add*, “Let's¦18154 not¦18153 \add take\add* his life¦18155.”
\v 22 “Don't¦18161 shed¦18163 blood¦18165,” he continued¦18157. “Throw¦18166 him into¦18168 \add that\add* pit¦18170 in¦18173 the¦18170 wilderness¦18173, but¦18157 don't¦18161 \add wound\add* him.” \add He said this\add* because he was¦18173 planning to¦18181 rescue¦18181 Yosef \add later\add* and¦18157 return him \add home\add* to \add their\add* father¦18187.
\v 23 \add So\add* when Yosef¦18193 \add reached\add* his¦18196 brothers¦18196, they¦18197 \add grabbed him and ripped\add* off the¦18206 coloured¦18207 robe¦18203 that¦18208 \add he was wearing\add*.
\v 24 Then¦18211 they¦18211 took¦18211 him and¦18211 \add dropped\add* him¦18211 into the pit. (The¦18213 pit was¦18216 empty¦18216 with no water¦18219 in¦18218 \add the bottom\add*).
\p
\v 25 Then¦18221 they¦18221 sat down to¦18222 eat¦18222, and \add a bit later when they looked up\add*, look, \add there was\add* a caravan¦18229 of¦18226 Yishma'elites¦18230 coming¦18231 \add towards them\add*. \add They had left\add* Gilead¦18232 carrying¦18239 spices¦18235 and¦18236 balm¦18236 and¦18237 myrrh¦18237 on their¦18226 camels¦18233 that they¦18238 were¦18238 going to¦18239 take¦18239 down¦18239 to Egypt¦18240.
\v 26 Then¦18242 Yehudah¦18243 \add !(Judah¦18243)\add* said¦18242 to¦18244 his brothers¦18246, “What¦18247 will¦18251 we gain¦18249 if we¦18251 kill¦18251 our¦18254 brother¦18254 and¦18242 cover¦18255 up his blood¦18258?
\v 27 Let's¦18261 sell¦18261 him¦18261 to¦18262 \add these\add* Ishmaelites¦18262 \add so we won't be guilty of killing\add* him¦18268. \add After all,\add* he's¦18273 our brother¦18271—our¦18271 \add own\add* flesh¦18272 \add and blood\add*.” And¦18261 his¦18275 brothers¦18275 \add agreed\add*.
\v 28 \add So when\add* the Midianite traders¦18280 came past, \add the brothers\add* pulled¦18281 Yosef up¦18282 and lifted¦18282 him out of the¦18288 pit¦18288 and¦18289 sold¦18289 \add him\add* to the Ishmaelites¦18293 for¦18294 twenty¦18294 \add pieces\add* of silver¦18295. Then¦18277 \add the traders took\add* Yosef \add onwards with them\add* to Mitsrayim¦18300.\x + \xo 37:28: \xt Acts 7:9.\x*
\p
\v 29 \add Later on,\add* Reuben¦18303 returned¦18302 to¦18304 the¦18306 pit¦18306, but¦18302 wow, Yosef¦18310 wasn't \add down there\add*, so he¦18312 tore¦18312 his¦18315 clothes¦18315 \add in despair\add*
\v 30 and¦18317 returned¦18317 to¦18318 his¦18320 brothers¦18320 and¦18321 said¦18321, “The¦18322 boy¦18322 isn't¦18323 there. \add What am I going to do\add*?”
\p
\v 31 Then¦18330 they¦18330 slaughtered¦18335 a young goat¦18336 and took¦18330 Yosef's¦18334 robe¦18341 and dipped¦18338 \add it\add* in¦18342 the¦18341 blood¦18342.
\v 32 Then¦18344 they¦18344 sent¦18344 the¦18347 coloured¦18348 robe \add back\add* to¦18350 their¦18352 father¦18352 with this¦18354 message: “We¦18355 found¦18355 this. Please¦18358 examine whether or¦18362 not¦18364 it's¦18361 your son's¦18360 robe.”
\p
\v 33 \add Yisra'el\add* recognised¦18366 it¦18366 and¦18366 said¦18367, “It¦18367 \em is¦18368\em* my¦18369 son's¦18369 robe¦18368. A \add wild\add* animal¦18370 \add must have eaten\add* him¦18372. Yosef¦18375 was \add almost\add* certainly torn¦18374 to¦18374 pieces¦18374.”
\v 34 Then¦18377 Yacob¦18378 ripped¦18377 his clothes¦18379 and¦18380 put¦18380 sackcloth¦18381 \add around\add* his¦18382 \add waist\add*, and¦18383 he¦18383 mourned¦18383 for his¦18386 son¦18386 many¦18388 days¦18387.
\v 35 All¦18391 his \add other\add* sons¦18393 and¦18394 all¦18394 his daughters¦18396 \add came\add* to¦18397 comfort¦18397 him, but¦18390 he¦18398 refused¦18398 to¦18399 be¦18399 comforted¦18399 and¦18400 said¦18400, “I¦18403 will¦18403 go¦18403 down¦18403 to¦18404 my¦18406 son¦18406 in \add the grave\add* mourning¦18407.” So¦18390 his father¦18411 wept¦18409 for¦18409 him¦18410.
\p
\v 36 Meanwhile, the¦18413 Midianites \add arrived\add* in¦18416 Egypt¦18418 and¦18413 sold¦18414 him¦18415 to¦18419 Potifar¦18419—Far'oh's¦18421 captain of¦18420 the guards¦18423.
\c 38
