\v 5 Then¦23001 Yacob¦23002 \add departed\add* from¦23003 Be'er¦23003-Sheva, and¦23005 \add his\add* sons¦23006 carried¦23005 their father¦23012 and¦23013 their¦23015 little¦23015 ones and¦23016 their wives¦23018 in¦23019 the¦23006 carts¦23019 that¦23020 Far'oh¦23023 had¦23022 sent¦23022 to¦23024 carry¦23024 him¦23025.
\v 6 They¦23027 \add had also brought along all\add* their livestock¦23030 and¦23031 their¦23033 possessions¦23033 that¦23034 they¦23035 had¦23035 acquired in¦23036 Canaan¦23037. Then¦23027 they¦23038 \add arrived in\add* Egypt¦23039—Yacob¦23040 and all of¦23030 his¦23043 offspring with¦23044 him¦23044:\x + \xo 46:6: \xt Acts 7:15.\x*
\v 7 his sons and his sons' sons with¦23049 him¦23049, and his daughters and¦23053 his sons' daughters. So he¦23056 brought¦23056 all¦23053 his offspring with¦23057 him¦23057 to Egypt¦23058.
\p
\v 8 These¦23061 are¦23062 the¦23062 names¦23062 of¦23062 Yisrael's¦23065 sons who¦23066 went¦23066 to¦23067 Egypt¦23067, \add that is\add* Yacob and¦23069 his¦23069 sons: \bd Yacob\bd*'s firstborn¦23070 was¦23062 Reuben¦23072,
