\v 27 \add As well as that\add*, Yosef's¦23297 two¦23305 sons¦23296 were¦23304 born¦23300 in¦23303 Egypt¦23303 so that¦23312 \add added up to a grand total of\add* seventy¦23314.\x + \xo 46:27: \xt Acts 7:14.\x*
\s1 Yacob's arrival in Egypt
\rem /s1 Jacob and His Family in Egypt; Jacob Settles in Goshen; Jacob's Family Arrives in Goshen
\p
\v 28 \add As they all approached Egypt, Yacob\add* sent¦23320 Yehudah¦23319 ahead¦23321 \add of the others\add* to¦23322 find out from Yosef¦23324 how to¦23325 get to¦23327 Goshen¦23327. \add As they all\add* arrived¦23328 in the Goshen¦23330 area,
\v 29 Yosef¦23333 \add hooked up\add* his chariot¦23334 and¦23335 went to¦23336 meet¦23336 his¦23339 father¦23339 Yisra'el¦23338 \add there\add*. He¦23340 \add went up to his father, and hugged him for a long time as he cried\add*.
\v 30 “Now I can die¦23358,” Yisra'el¦23354 said¦23353 to¦23355 Yosef¦23357, “since I've¦23361 seen¦23361 your¦23364 face¦23364—\add seen\add* that¦23359 you're¦23366 still¦23366 alive¦23367.”
\p
\v 31 Then¦23369 Yosef¦23370 spoke¦23369 to¦23371 his brothers and¦23374 to¦23374 his¦23377 father's¦23377 household, “I'll¦23378 go¦23378 and¦23379 report¦23379 to¦23380 Far'oh¦23380 and¦23381 \add explain\add* to¦23382 him¦23382 that my brothers and¦23384 my¦23386 father's¦23386 household who¦23387 were living in¦23388 Canaan¦23390 have¦23391 come¦23391 to¦23392 \add join\add* me¦23392.
\v 32 \add I'll tell him that you're\add* herders of¦23395 sheep¦23396—livestock¦23400 \add farmers\add*—and¦23402 \add that you've\add* brought¦23408 your flocks¦23402 and¦23403 herds¦23403 and¦23404 everything that¦23406 \add you own\add*.
\v 33 So¦23411 when Far'oh¦23415 calls for¦23414 you¦23414 and¦23416 \add asks what your work is\add*,
\v 34 then¦23421 you should¦23437 \add answer\add*, ‘Your¦23436 servants¦23425 have¦23424 been¦23424 livestock¦23423 men¦23422 from our youth¦23426 and¦23427 until now¦23429, both¦23430 we¦23432 and also¦23427 our fathers¦23435,’ so that you can settle¦23437 \add here\add* in¦23436 Goshen¦23439, because¦23440 Egyptians¦23443 \add despise sheep herders\add*.”
\c 47
\rem /s1 Jacob Blesses Pharaoh
\p
\v 1 Then¦23449 went¦23449 Yosef¦23450 to¦23452 Far'oh¦23452 and told¦23451 \add him\add*, “My¦23454 father¦23454 and¦23455 brothers¦23455 and¦23456 their¦23456 flocks¦23456 and¦23457 herds¦23457 and¦23458 everything that¦23460 \add belongs\add* to¦23461 them¦23461, have¦23462 come¦23462 from¦23463 Canaan¦23464 and¦23465 they're \add here now\add* Goshen¦23467 \add area\add*.”
\v 2 Then¦23469 he¦23471 took¦23471 five¦23472 of¦23475 his brothers¦23470 and¦23469 presented¦23474 them¦23474 to¦23475 Far'oh¦23476,
\v 3 and¦23486 Far'oh¦23479 \add asked them\add*, “What's¦23483 your¦23492 occupation¦23485?”
\p “Your¦23492 servants¦23492 have been shepherds \add for several generations\add*,” they¦23486 \add ≈replied¦23478\add*.
\v 4 Then¦23500 they¦23500 \add explained\add*, “We've¦23503 come¦23506 to¦23501 \add stay here for a while\add* because in¦23518 Canaan¦23519, there's¦23509 no pasture¦23510 for¦23511 our flocks¦23511 because \add the drought is very severe\add*. So¦23500 now¦23520, please¦23523 let¦23521 your¦23524 servants¦23524 settle¦23521 in¦23525 the Goshen¦23526 \add area\add*.”
\v 5 Then¦23528 Far'oh¦23529 turned to¦23530 Yosef¦23532, “Your¦23534 father¦23534 and¦23535 your¦23535 brothers¦23535 have¦23536 come¦23536 to¦23537 you¦23537.
\v 6 The¦23543 \add entire country\add* of Egypt¦23540 is¦23558 in front¦23541 of you. Settle your father¦23548 and¦23549 your brothers¦23551 in the best¦23543 land¦23553, \add so\add* let¦23552 them¦23552 settle in¦23553 the Goshen¦23554 \add area\add*. And¦23555 if¦23555 you're \add aware\add* that¦23569 \add some of them have special talents\add*, then appoint¦23564 them¦23564 as overseers¦23565 of¦23565 \add my own\add* livestock¦23566 \add as well\add*.”
\p
\v 7 Then¦23573 Yosef¦23574 brought¦23573 his¦23578 father¦23578 Yacob and¦23579 presented¦23579 him¦23579 to¦23580 Far'oh, and¦23582 Yacob blessed¦23582 Far'oh.
\v 8 “How¦23592 \add old are you\add*?” Far'oh¦23589 asked¦23588 him.
\p
\v 9 “\add I've been moving from place to place for\add* 130 years¦23608,” Yacob¦23599 \add ≈replied¦23598\add*. “\add My life has been short and with many difficulties, so I\add* haven't reached¦23616 the¦23619 longer \add ages of my ancestors in their moving around\add*.”
\v 10 Then¦23626 \add he\add* blessed¦23626 Far'oh¦23630 \add again\add* and¦23631 departed¦23631 from¦23632 \add his\add* presence¦23632.
\v 11 So¦23635 Yosef¦23636 gave¦23643 his father¦23639 and¦23640 his brothers¦23642 \add some of the best land\add* in¦23646 Egypt¦23647 and \add helped\add* them¦23644 settle¦23635 there—in¦23648 the Rameses¦23651 \add district just\add* as¦23652 Far'oh¦23654 had¦23653 commanded¦23653.
\v 12 \add He also\add* provided¦23656 his¦23660 father¦23660 and¦23661 his brothers¦23663 and¦23664 all¦23665 his¦23668 father's¦23668 household¦23667 with bread¦23669—each¦23665 family¦23667 according¦23670 to¦23670 the¦23670 \add number of children\add*.
\s1 Yosef's leadership through extreme famine
\rem /s1 Joseph's Leadership in the Famine; Joseph and the Famine; The Famine; The Famine in Egypt
\p
\v 13 \add Then the time came when\add* there¦23674 was no bread¦23673 in¦23675 \add that entire part of\add* the¦23677 world¦23677, because¦23678 the \add drought\add* was now extremely severe, and¦23683 \add both\add* Egypt¦23685 and¦23686 Canaan¦23687 were \add suffering from food shortages\add*.
\v 14 \add People all over came\add* to buy¦23708 grain¦23704, and \add over time\add* Yosef¦23692 had received \add in payment\add* all¦23695 the¦23697 silver that¦23705 could be found¦23698 in¦23699 Egypt¦23701 and¦23702 Canaan¦23703, and¦23709 \add he in turn\add* took¦23709 it¦23709 to¦23714 Far'oh's¦23715 house¦23714.
\v 15 So¦23717 \add once there was no more silver left\add* in Egypt¦23720 and¦23717 in Canaan¦23722, all¦23724 \add the Egyptians\add* demanded from¦23719 Yosef¦23729, “Give us food¦23734. Why should we¦23736 die¦23736 \add right here in front of\add* you¦23737? \add All our money\add* is¦23717 gone!”
\p
\v 16 “Bring your¦23748 livestock¦23745,” Yosef¦23743 \add ≈answered¦23742\add*, “and¦23742 I'll give¦23746 grain to¦23747 you in¦23748 exchange for¦23747 \add them\add*, since the silver is gone.”
\v 17 So \add the people\add* brought¦23754 their livestock to¦23758 \add him\add*, and¦23761 \add he\add* gave¦23761 them¦23762 grain \add in exchange for their\add* horses¦23765 and¦23766 sheep¦23767 and¦23768 cattle¦23769 and¦23770 donkeys¦23770. So he¦23771 provided¦23771 them with¦23765 food¦23772 that¦23777 year¦23776 \add in exchange\add* for all¦23773 their livestock.
\p
\v 18 \add The next\add* year¦23780 they¦23782 came¦23782 to¦23783 \add Yosef\add* and¦23786 \add begged\add*, “We¦23790 can't¦23788 hide¦23790 it¦23795 from¦23791 our master¦23791 that¦23792 since \add there's no silver left\add* and¦23797 \add since all\add* the¦23797 livestock¦23797 \add now\add* belongs to¦23799 our lord, there's nothing left¦23803 \add to offer other than\add* our bodies¦23809 and our lands¦23810.
\v 19 Why should¦23835 we die \add right in front of you\add*—both we and our land? Buy¦23820 us¦23822 and¦23823 our land in exchange for¦23826 food¦23826, and¦23827 we¦23827 and our land will¦23827 be¦23827 slaves¦23830 to¦23812 Far'oh¦23831. And¦23829 give¦23832 us seed¦23834 so that we'll¦23827 live¦23835 and¦23836 not¦23836 die¦23837, and¦23838 so that the¦23838 land won't¦23836 be¦23840 barren.”
\p
\v 20 So¦23842 Yosef¦23843 bought¦23842 all¦23846 the¦23848 farmland of¦23848 Egypt¦23849 for¦23850 Far'oh¦23864, because every¦23855 Egyptian¦23854 sold¦23853 his¦23856 field¦23856. \add In that way, all\add* the¦23863 land¦23863 became¦23862 Far'oh's¦23850 because the¦23861 famine¦23861 was¦23859 \add so extreme\add*.
\v 21 \add As for\add* the¦23868 people¦23868, he¦23869 moved them to¦23871 the cities¦23871\f + \fr 47:21 \ft TC: There's a variation here in different early copies and translations. Rather than moving the people into the cities (which might have been done to make food distribution more efficient), some translations choose the alternative ‘made the people slaves’.\f* from¦23872 one end¦23872 of¦23872 Egypt¦23875 to¦23876 the other¦23878.
\v 22 The¦23881 only¦23880 land¦23881 he¦23884 didn't buy¦23884 was that¦23894 of¦23881 the¦23882 priests¦23882, because¦23885 they \add were given a regular allowance\add* by Far'oh¦23889. Because¦23897 they \add could live on what they were supplied with\add*, they didn't \add need to\add* sell¦23902 their¦23905 land.
\v 23 Then¦23907 Yosef¦23908 told¦23907 the¦23911 people¦23911, “Listen, now that I've¦23913 bought¦23913 you and¦23907 your land¦23918 for¦23919 Far'oh¦23919, here¦23920 is¦23923 seed¦23923 for you so that you can \add work\add* the ground¦23918.
\v 24 \add Every time\add* you harvest¦23930 \add a crop\add*, you must¦23931 give¦23931 a fifth¦23932 \add of it\add* to¦23933 Far'oh¦23933. The¦23935 \add other\add* four¦23934 parts¦23935 will¦23936 be for¦23937 you \add to use\add* as seed¦23938 and¦23940 as food¦23940 for yourselves¦23940 and¦23941 your households¦23942 and¦23943 your¦23944 young¦23944 children.”
\p
\v 25 “You've kept¦23947 us¦23947 alive¦23947,” they¦23946 \add agreed\add*. “Master¦23952, \add continue to show us your favour\add*, and¦23953 we'll¦23953 be¦23953 slaves¦23954 for Far'oh¦23955.”
\v 26 So¦23957 Yosef¦23959 established¦23957 it¦23957 as a¦23960 law to this¦23964 day¦23963 concerning the¦23964 Egyptian¦23968 farmland: that¦23964 the¦23967 fifth¦23970 belongs¦23976 to¦23977 Far'oh¦23977. (Only¦23971 the¦23972 priests' land¦23972 didn't¦23975 become Far'oh's¦23969.)
\s1 Yacob's burial request
\rem /s1 Jacob's Last Request; The Last Days of Jacob
\p
\v 27 So¦23979 Yisra'el¦23980 \add !(Yacob) and his descendants\add* settled in the Goshen¦23984 region¦23981 of¦23982 Egypt¦23982 and \add prospered\add*. The \add had many children\add* and \add quickly increased in number\add*.
\v 28 Yacob¦23992 resided \add there\add* for seventeen¦23995 years, and¦23991 \add by then\add* he¦23991 was¦23998 147 years old
\v 29 and¦24010 he was getting close¦24010 to¦24015 death¦24015, so he¦24016 called¦24016 for his¦24018 son¦24018 Yosef¦24019 and¦24020 asked¦24020 him¦24021, “If¦24022, please¦24024, I¦24025 have¦24025 found¦24025 favour¦24026 in¦24027 your eyes¦24027, please \add give me your hand and promise to\add* deal with¦24027 me¦24035 in kindness¦24036 and¦24037 faithfulness¦24037. Please¦24040 don't¦24038 bury¦24041 me¦24041 in¦24042 Egypt¦24042.\x + \xo 47:29-30: \xt Gen 49:29-32; 50:6.\x*
\v 30 When¦24044 I \add die\add*, I want to¦24055 be buried¦24050 with¦24051 my¦24047 ancestors¦24047, so carry¦24048 me¦24048 out of¦24051 Egypt¦24049 and¦24044 bury¦24050 me¦24050 in¦24051 their¦24051 tomb¦24051.”
\p “I'll¦24054 do¦24054 \add what you've requested\add*,” Yosef \add agreed\add*.
\p
\v 31 “Promise me¦24059,” he¦24057 \add insisted\add*. So¦24057 \add Yosef promised\add* him¦24061 and¦24057 Yisra'el¦24063 bowed¦24062 at¦24064 the¦24066 head¦24066 of¦24066 the¦24067 bed¦24067.\f + \fr 47:31 \ft Some translations assume that elderly Yacob/Yisra'el bowed to God in worship after speaking with Yosef, but it's not impossible that he bowed to Yosef in acknowledgement of the high position that God had brought Yosef to as foretold by his dreams.\f*
\c 48
\s1 Yacob blesses Efrayim and Menashsheh
\rem /s1 Jacob Blesses Manasseh and Ephraim; Jacob Blesses Joseph's Sons; Jacob Blesses Ephraim and Manasseh; Manasseh and Ephraim
\p
\v 1 Some time after¦24071 that, Yosef was¦24070 told¦24074, “Listen, your¦24077 father¦24077 is¦24078 sick¦24078.” So Yosef \add went to him\add*, taking¦24079 his¦24083 two¦24082 sons¦24083 with¦24084 him¦24084—Manasseh¦24087 and¦24088 Efrayim¦24090.
\v 2 When¦24101 someone¦24092 told¦24092 Yacob¦24093 that Yosef¦24097 had¦24098 arrived¦24098, \add he\add* exerted himself¦24100 and¦24092 sat¦24102 up in bed¦24105,
\v 3 then¦24107 he¦24107 told¦24107 him, “God¦24112 the provider appeared¦24114 to¦24109 me¦24116 at¦24117 Luz¦24117 in¦24117 Canaan¦24119, and¦24107 he blessed¦24120 me¦24121\x + \xo 48:3-4: \xt Gen 28:13-14.\x*
\v 4 and¦24123 said¦24123 to¦24124 me¦24124, ‘Listen, I'll make¦24126 you¦24126 fruitful¦24126, and¦24127 I'll multiply¦24127 you¦24127 and¦24128 make¦24128 you¦24128 into¦24129 a community of¦24129 peoples¦24130. And¦24131 I'll give¦24131 this¦24135 land¦24134 to your¦24126 offspring¦24136 after¦24137 you to be¦24126 their possession¦24138 forever¦24139.’
\v 5 “And¦24141 now¦24141, your¦24144 two¦24142 sons¦24144, who¦24145 were¦24145 born¦24145 for¦24146 you¦24152 \add here\add* in¦24147 Egypt¦24148 before I came¦24151 \add here\add*, I \add adopt\add* them as my own—Efrayim¦24157 and¦24158 Manasseh¦24158—just as¦24159 Reuben¦24159 and¦24160 Simeon¦24160 are¦24145 mine.
\v 6 \add Any other\add* children¦24165 that you¦24168 father¦24168 after¦24169 them¦24169 will be¦24175 yours¦24170. Their¦24176 inheritance¦24176 will \add only be through their older\add* brothers¦24174.
\v 7 As for me¦24183, \add when\add* I was coming¦24180 into¦24185 Canaan¦24186 from Paddan¦24181, Rahel¦24184 died¦24182 beside on¦24180 the way when we were still¦24188 quite some distance¦24189 from Efrath, and¦24178 I buried¦24194 her¦24194 there¦24195 beside the¦24196 road of¦24196 Efrath¦24197 (which¦24198 is¦24199 Bethlehem).”\x + \xo 48:7: \xt Gen 35:16-19.\x*
\p
\v 8 Then¦24202 Yisra'el¦24203 \add noticed\add* Yosef's¦24207 \add two\add* sons¦24206 and¦24208 \add asked\add*, “Who¦24209 are¦24211 these¦24211?”
\p
\v 9 “They¦24219 are¦24218 my¦24218 sons¦24218 that¦24226 God¦24225 has¦24222 given¦24222 me¦24224 \add here\add* in¦24226 this¦24226 place¦24226.” Yosef¦24214 \add ≈replied¦24213\add* to¦24231 his¦24217 father¦24217.
\p “Please¦24230 bring¦24228 them to me, and¦24213 I¦24232 will¦24218 bless¦24232 them¦24232,” \add Yacob requested\add*.
\v 10 Now Yisra'el's¦24235 sight¦24234 was¦24239 poor in his old¦24237 age¦24237, so he¦24239 wasn't able¦24239 to¦24240 see¦24240 \add much\add*. So¦24234 \add Yosef\add* brought¦24241 them¦24242 over to¦24243 him¦24243, and¦24244 \add Yisra'el\add* kissed¦24244 them¦24245 and¦24246 embraced¦24246 them¦24247.
\v 11 “I¦24257 \add never expected to see you again\add*” \add he\add* said¦24249 to¦24251 Yosef¦24253, “but¦24249 wow¦24254, God¦24261 has¦24259 \add even\add* let me¦24260 see¦24259 your¦24265 children¦24265 as well.”
\v 12 Then¦24269 Yosef¦24268 removed¦24267 \add his sons\add* from¦24270 his \add father's\add* knees¦24271 and¦24272 bowed¦24272 with¦24270 his¦24271 face¦24273 to¦24273 the¦24274 ground¦24274.
